<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch Q3 GDP confirmed at rise of 3.0 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Dutch Q3 GDP confirmed at rise of 3.0 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch third quarter gross domestic product (GDP) rose 3.0 percent year-on-year, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said, confirming provisional figures released in November.</p>
<p>DUTCH GDP IN DETAIL</p>
<p> (real pct change yr/yr)		Q3 96  Q2 96  Q1 96  Q4 95</p>
<p> private consumption			2.6    3.0    3.5    2.0</p>
<p> government consumption		   0.7    0.5    0.6    0.7</p>
<p> business investment			8.5    2.7   -1.6    3.2</p>
<p> government investment		    5.9    6.9   -6.1    0.3</p>
<p> exports goods and services	     5.5    0.9    4.3    6.4</p>
<p> imports goods and services	     5.2    0.9    2.7    4.3</p>
<p>DUTCH GDP - INVESTMENT IN DETAIL</p>
<p> (real pct change yr/yr)		Q3 96  Q2 96  Q1 96  Q4 95</p>
<p> total gross fixed investment	   8.1    3.2   -2.2    2.7</p>
<p> housing					2.4    2.9  -17.7   -3.9</p>
<p> other buildings			    5.1   13.0  -13.2    0.3</p>
<p> roads, waterways etc.		    5.8    8.4   -5.8    4.7</p>
<p> transport equipment			0.9  -13.1   -0.6   -0.5</p>
<p> machinery				   17.3    0.7   11.6   12.7</p>
<p>CBS said third quarter investments in machinery had been boosted by the taking into production of two new units at the Eems power plant in the northern Netherlands.</p>
<p>It said that excluding the impact of strongly fluctuating investments in aeroplanes, shipping and major projects such as the Eems plant, total gross fixed investment would have risen by some six percent.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
